{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md | sed -n '123,285p'\"","aggregated_output":"   123\t## Publishing and loading code over the DHT\n   124\t\n   125\tWith `--index-store dht:<dir>` the code index is the durable, exclusively\n   126\tlocked directory store with a `dao.space.dht` node composed over it: the\n   127\tnode joins the DHT, shares the store's content when told to, and fetches\n   128\twhat a `require` asks for and the node does not hold. The `--dht-*`\n   129\tflags are refused with any other store, with one exception:\n   130\t`--dht-keygen` composes nothing, writes its key file, and exits, so it\n   131\tneeds no `--index-store` at all.\n   132\t\n   133\t**The flags.** `--dht-peer host:port` (repeatable) names the bootstrap\n   134\tcontacts; the host must be an IP literal, and no peer means a solo node\n   135\tthat opens no socket, whose publications stay durable in the directory\n   136\tand acknowledged by no one. `--dht-publish` shares everything the\n   137\tdirectory holds with any peer that asks for an address; without it the\n   138\tnode fetches only. `--dht-bind ip` and `--dht-port p` set the socket's\n   139\taddress, loopback and ephemeral unless given, and need a peer;\n   140\t`--dht-max-inbound-bytes n` bounds the payload the node accepts from\n   141\tpeers, 64 MiB by default. `--dht-manifest :segment/...`, with or without\n   142\tits leading colon, hands the node a remote index manifest to hydrate\n   143\tbefore the first evaluation, and needs a peer too. `--dht-key file` loads\n   144\tthe publisher's stable Ed25519 key file, and `--dht-principal hex`\n   145\t(repeatable) declares a publisher whose signed names this node honors:\n   146\tthe public key's 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits alone, without the\n   147\t`ed25519:` prefix the banner prints before them. `--dht-keygen file`\n   148\twrites a new key file, from the host CSPRNG, and exits with status 0.\n   149\tA bind that fails, or a hydration that cannot complete, refuses the\n   150\tshell with exit status 1 instead of composing over an empty index.\n   151\t\n   152\t```bash\n   153\tclj -M:clj-yin-repl --index-store dht:/tmp/yin-a --dht-peer 127.0.0.1:4001 \\\n   154\t    --dht-publish --dht-key /tmp/yin-a.key\n   155\t```\n   156\t\n   157\tThe banner states, before the node steps once and so before anything is\n   158\tshared, what will be shared: that publishing is on and everything in the\n   159\tdirectory's content path will be shared, or that the node fetches only.\n   160\tWith `--dht-key` it also names the principal that signs every name\n   161\tpublished here, as `ed25519:` before the very digits `--dht-principal`\n   162\ttakes (`dht: names published here are signed by principal ed25519:...\n   163\t(key from <file>)`); without one, that `(yin.link/publish ...)` is\n   164\trefused while names are still read, resolved, loaded and linked. The\n   165\tnode's first ticks print where the socket bound (`dht: node ...\n   166\tlistening on 127.0.0.1:53812; peers: ...; publishing`, or `fetch-only`).\n   167\t\n   168\t**Publishing a module by signed name.** `(require (quote yin.link))`\n   169\tinstalls the host module. `(yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))`\n   170\tderives the module from this session's indexed code, so every export\n   171\tmust already be defined at the prompt: an export with no defining\n   172\tprogram refuses `:yin.link.publish/undefined-export`. The defining\n   173\tprograms of the exports and, to a fixed point, of the free names they\n   174\tread are minted into all four code formats under one schema-1 manifest\n   175\tand materialized into the index store content-addressed. The answer\n   176\tnames the module, its manifest address, and the linker's own verdict per\n   177\tformat:\n   178\t\n   179\t```clojure\n   180\tyin> (def f (fn [x] (+ x 4200)))\n   181\tyin> (require (quote yin.link))\n   182\tyin> (yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))\n   183\t{:module 'my.lib, :address :segment/..., :links {...}}\n   184\t```\n   185\t\n   186\tThe name binding is a set of Ed25519-signed envelopes binding the name to\n   187\tthat manifest address, committed through the session's indexer as one\n   188\ttransaction whose HEAD write announces the publication. The node then\n   189\treports the result: `dht: published :segment/... (N blobs)` followed by\n   190\t`acknowledged: sent to N peers`, or a PARTIAL or NOT acknowledged line\n   191\tnaming the count of blobs not sent, the first reason, and whether it is\n   192\tretrying. A retrying publication repairs in the background while the\n   193\tnode is open; a line that says `not retrying` will not repair: a\n   194\tpublication with no retryable failures is final, and an older repair can\n   195\tbe displaced by a newer one. Republishing a name at another manifest\n   196\tretracts the standing assertion first. `:links` is per format,\n   197\tand a format it refused at publish time (an export reading a module-level\n   198\tdefinition from inside a lambda refuses the tree format) refuses at\n   199\trequire time too.\n   200\t\n   201\t**Loading it in another yin.repl.** Start the reader against a peer, with\n   202\tthe publisher's index manifest and its principal:\n   203\t\n   204\t```bash\n   205\tclj -M:clj-yin-repl --index-store dht:/tmp/yin-b --dht-peer 127.0.0.1:53812 \\\n   206\t    --dht-manifest :segment/... --dht-principal 9d61b19d...\n   207\t```\n   208\t\n   209\tThe principal on the command line is the publisher's 64 hex digits\n   210\talone, without the banner's `ed25519:` prefix. Hydration runs before the\n   211\tfirst evaluation: typed lines wait in the input\n   212\tmedium until the reader prints `dht: hydrated :<manifest>`, with the\n   213\tdatom and blob counts, and `evaluation admitted`. Then require by name:\n   214\t\n   215\t```clojure\n   216\tyin> (require (quote my.lib))\n   217\t;; require pending: my.lib (link N); lines typed meanwhile ...\n   218\tyin> 'my.lib\n   219\tyin> (my.lib/f 1)\n   220\t4201\n   221\t```\n   222\t\n   223\tA require whose closure the node does not hold prints the\n   224\t`;; require pending: ...` line and parks: the node fetches the module's\n   225\tclosure from the peers, the parked require is re-checked when the load\n   226\tends, lines typed meanwhile run when it completes, and `(abandon)` gives\n   227\tit up. The require answers the module's name and the export evaluates.\n   228\tEach VM's session links the module itself, so after `(vm :type)` require\n   229\tthe name again: the same published name evaluates on all four VMs.\n   230\t`(yin.link/names)` answers the names this node resolves, each with its\n   231\tmanifest address and the principal that asserted it.\n   232\t\n   233\t**Why a required name can be trusted.** Content is content-addressed,\n   234\tand every hop re-verifies it: a blob fetched from a peer is checked\n   235\tagainst the address it was asked for before it enters the local store,\n   236\tand the closure walk re-checks the manifest, every tree row, every\n   237\tderivation record and every image against its own address. A manifest\n   238\tlinks at a name only if it declares that name. Names resolve only from\n   239\tsigned assertions of declared principals: an undeclared publisher, or a\n   240\tproof that does not verify, refuses the require `:absent` with the\n   241\treasons as data. The same address asserted by several declared\n   242\tprincipals resolves with every asserter named; two distinct addresses\n   243\trefuse `:ambiguous-name`. A failed load is refused and forgotten, so a\n   244\tlater require starts a new load. The link source reads only the node's\n   245\town store, and the directory's lock keeps one owner per directory. A\n   246\tretraction whose target no loaded snapshot holds is reported once,\n   247\tglobally, by `(yin.link/names)`, never as a per-name diagnostic.\n   248\t`docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md` is the contract for all of it.\n   249\t\n   250\t**The plain-Clojure path.** A non-REPL client takes the same path through\n   251\tplain functions: `dao.space.dht/join` over a store, `load-index` for a\n   252\tmanifest address (step the node with `dao.space.dht/step`; `load-status`\n   253\tanswers `:loading`, `:loaded`, or `:failed` with the reason as data),\n   254\t`yin.vm.linker.dht/names` to resolve names under an authority of\n   255\tdeclared principals (`yin.vm.linker.dht/authority`),\n   256\t`yin.vm.linker.dht/load-module` for a module's closure, and\n   257\t`yin.vm.linker.dht/link` for one format's image; every failure answers\n   258\tthe data of that design's section 9. At the prompt,\n   259\t`(require (quote dao.space.dht))` answers `load-index`, `load-status`,\n   260\t`q`, `retry`, `cancel`, `load-module` and `module-status` as host\n   261\tfunctions over the shell's own node; the name fold itself is the\n   262\tprompt's `(yin.link/names)`.\n   263\t\n   264\t**Operational notes.** Keep the key file: a lost key can never sign\n   265\tagain, and a new key is a new principal. Receivers verify names against\n   266\tthe publisher's principal, not against where the bytes came from, so\n   267\thand the principal out with the network address and replace the\n   268\tdeclaration when a key rotates. The Node reader the process tests spawn\n   269\tis a build artifact: `bb build:yin-repl-node` writes `target/yin-repl.js`,\n   270\tand a missing build fails `test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj`. A fresh\n   271\tworktree must run `clj -M:antlr-gen` before JVM test runs: the generated\n   272\tparser path, `build/antlr/python3/classes`, is on the classpath and\n   273\tabsent until generated.\n   274\t\n   275\tSee [`docs/design/yin.repl.implementation-plan.md`](../../../../docs/design/yin.repl.implementation-plan.md)\n   276\tfor the plan this REPL implements and the contract documents it is subordinate\n   277\tto.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '97,112p;204,237p;246,320p;360,391p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '918,975p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '138,155p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '340,350p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc | sed -n '175,182p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '88,123p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '97,112p;204,237p;246,320p;360,391p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '918,975p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '138,155p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '340,350p'; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc | sed -n '175,182p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '88,123p'\"","aggregated_output":"    97\t(def ^:private dht-flags\n    98\t  #{\"--dht-peer\" \"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-bind\" \"--dht-port\"\n    99\t    \"--dht-max-inbound-bytes\" \"--dht-manifest\" \"--dht-key\" \"--dht-principal\"})\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(defn parse-principal\n   103\t  \"A `--dht-principal` value: a declared publisher's public key, exactly\n   104\t   64 lowercase hexadecimal characters (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.2).\"\n   105\t  [text]\n   106\t  (if (and (string? text) (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" text))\n   107\t    text\n   108\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-principal takes a public key of 64 lowercase \"\n   109\t                         \"hexadecimal characters, not \" (pr-str text))\n   110\t                    {:value text}))))\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   204\t(defn- dht-spec\n   205\t  \"Fold the `--dht-*` flags into the `dht:<dir>` spec, checked by\n   206\t   `yin.repl.store/checked-spec`.  They mean nothing to any other store,\n   207\t   and a bind address means nothing to a solo node, so each such use is\n   208\t   refused rather than ignored.\"\n   209\t  [spec {:keys [flags peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n   210\t                manifest]}]\n   211\t  (cond\n   212\t    (and (seq flags) (not= :dht (:type spec)))\n   213\t    (throw (ex-info (str (str/join \", \" (sort flags))\n   214\t                         \" need --index-store dht:<dir>\")\n   215\t                    {:flags (vec (sort flags))}))\n   216\t\n   217\t    (not= :dht (:type spec)) spec\n   218\t\n   219\t    (and (empty? peers) (or bind-host bind-port))\n   220\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-bind and --dht-port need a --dht-peer: \"\n   221\t                         \"with no peers the DHT store is solo and opens \"\n   222\t                         \"no socket\")\n   223\t                    {}))\n   224\t\n   225\t    (and bind-host (not (datagram/ip-literal? bind-host)))\n   226\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-bind must be an IP literal, not \"\n   227\t                         (pr-str bind-host))\n   228\t                    {:value bind-host}))\n   229\t\n   230\t    :else\n   231\t    (store/checked-spec\n   232\t      (cond-> (assoc spec :peers (vec peers) :publish? (boolean publish?))\n   233\t        bind-host (assoc :bind-host bind-host)\n   234\t        bind-port (assoc :bind-port bind-port)\n   235\t        max-inbound-bytes (assoc :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes)\n   236\t        manifest (assoc :manifest manifest)))))\n   237\t\n   246\t(defn parse-args\n   247\t  \"Parse the host arguments.  `--telemetry` and `--telemetry-stream` are\n   248\t   rejected rather than ignored.  `--index-store` is parsed into\n   249\t   `:index-store-spec` — `:mem` (also what omission means),\n   250\t   `{:type :file :dir dir}`, or the DHT store `{:type :dht :dir dir ...}`\n   251\t   — and a missing value, an unknown scheme, or an empty directory is\n   252\t   refused here, by `yin.repl.store/parse-arg`, before any host composes.\n   253\t\n   254\t   The DHT store's options are their own flags (yin.repl.dht):\n   255\t   `--dht-peer host:port`, repeatable, the bootstrap contacts — none\n   256\t   means solo, with no socket; `--dht-publish`, the separate declaration\n   257\t   that shares the store; `--dht-bind ip` and `--dht-port p`, the\n   258\t   socket's address, loopback and ephemeral unless given;\n   259\t   `--dht-max-inbound-bytes n`, the inbound storage bound; and\n   260\t   `--dht-manifest address`, a remote index to hydrate before the first\n   261\t   evaluation; `--dht-key file`, the publisher's stable key file\n   262\t   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.5); and `--dht-principal hex`, repeatable, a\n   263\t   publisher whose signed names this node honors (7.1).  Any of them\n   264\t   without `dht:<dir>` is refused.  `--dht-keygen file` writes a new key\n   265\t   file and exits.\"\n   266\t  [args]\n   267\t  (loop [args (seq args)\n   268\t         opts {:headless? false :host nil :port nil :rejected []\n   269\t               :index-store-spec :mem}\n   270\t         dht {:flags #{} :peers []}]\n   271\t    (if-let [arg (first args)]\n   272\t      (let [dht (cond-> dht (dht-flags arg) (update :flags conj arg))\n   273\t            value (second args)]\n   274\t        (case arg\n   275\t          \"--port\" (recur (nnext args)\n   276\t                          (assoc opts :port (when-let [p (second args)]\n   277\t                                              #?(:cljd (int/parse p)\n   278\t                                                 :cljs (js/parseInt p 10)\n   279\t                                                 :clj (Long/parseLong p))))\n   280\t                          dht)\n   281\t          \"--host\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc opts :host (second args)) dht)\n   282\t          \"--headless\" (recur (next args) (assoc opts :headless? true) dht)\n   283\t          \"--index-store\" (recur (nnext args)\n   284\t                                 (assoc opts\n   285\t                                        :index-store-spec\n   286\t                                        (store/parse-arg (second args)))\n   287\t                                 dht)\n   288\t          \"--dht-peer\" (recur (nnext args) opts\n   289\t                              (update dht :peers conj (parse-peer value)))\n   290\t          \"--dht-publish\" (recur (next args) opts (assoc dht :publish? true))\n   291\t          \"--dht-bind\" (recur (nnext args) opts\n   292\t                              (assoc dht :bind-host (str value)))\n   293\t          \"--dht-port\" (recur (nnext args) opts\n   294\t                              (assoc dht :bind-port (dht-number arg value)))\n   295\t          \"--dht-max-inbound-bytes\" (recur (nnext args) opts\n   296\t                                           (assoc dht :max-inbound-bytes\n   297\t                                                  (dht-number arg value)))\n   298\t          \"--dht-manifest\" (recur (nnext args) opts\n   299\t                                  (assoc dht :manifest (parse-manifest value)))\n   300\t          \"--dht-key\" (recur (nnext args)\n   301\t                             (assoc opts :dht-key-file\n   302\t                                    (or value\n   303\t                                        (throw (ex-info \"--dht-key needs a key file\"\n   304\t                                                        {}))))\n   305\t                             dht)\n   306\t          \"--dht-principal\" (recur (nnext args)\n   307\t                                   (update opts :principals (fnil conj [])\n   308\t                                           (parse-principal value))\n   309\t                                   dht)\n   310\t          \"--dht-keygen\" (recur (nnext args)\n   311\t                                (assoc opts :dht-keygen\n   312\t                                       (or value\n   313\t                                           (throw (ex-info \"--dht-keygen needs a file\"\n   314\t                                                           {}))))\n   315\t                                dht)\n   316\t          \"--telemetry\" (recur (next args) (update opts :rejected conj arg) dht)\n   317\t          \"--telemetry-stream\" (recur (nnext args)\n   318\t                                      (update opts :rejected conj arg) dht)\n   319\t          (recur (next args) (update opts :extra (fnil conj []) arg) dht)))\n   320\t      (update opts :index-store-spec dht-spec dht))))\n   360\t   `--dht-keygen` composes nothing: it writes the key file and answers\n   361\t   `{:lines [...] :exit 0}` for the host to print and exit with.  A\n   362\t   `--dht-key` file is loaded here (`load-key`); the key reaches the\n   363\t   shell, and only its principal reaches the options the banner reads.\"\n   364\t  [args]\n   365\t  (try\n   366\t    (let [opts (parse-args args)]\n   367\t      (if-some [path (:dht-keygen opts)]\n   368\t        (keygen! path)\n   369\t        (let [key (some-> (:dht-key-file opts) load-key)\n   370\t              opts (cond-> opts\n   371\t                     key (assoc :publisher (sign/principal (:public key))))]\n   372\t          {:opts opts\n   373\t           :state (boot (assoc opts :dht-key key))\n   374\t           :server (boot-server opts)})))\n   375\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object\n   376\t              :clj Throwable\n   377\t              :cljs :default)\n   378\t           e\n   379\t      (if (ex-data e)\n   380\t        {:refusal (or (ex-message e) (str e))}\n   381\t        (throw e)))))\n   382\t\n   383\t\n   384\t(defn- refuse!\n   385\t  \"Print why the composition refused to start and end the process with a\n   386\t   failing status, so a refused startup never looks like a working shell.\"\n   387\t  [refusal]\n   388\t  (println refusal)\n   389\t  #?(:cljd (io/exit 1)\n   390\t     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 1)\n   391\t     :cljs (.exit js/process 1)))\n   918\t(defn- ending\n   919\t  [pub]\n   920\t  (or (:ended pub)\n   921\t      (when (and (not= :acknowledged (result pub)) (zero? (:retryable pub)))\n   922\t        ::terminal)))\n   923\t\n   924\t\n   925\t(defn- evaluate\n   926\t  \"One publication's report this step, if any: `[pub' event-or-nil\n   927\t   retire?]`.\"\n   928\t  [node pub]\n   929\t  (cond\n   930\t    (:cancelled? pub)\n   931\t    (let [pub (assoc pub :ended ::cancelled)]\n   932\t      [pub (report (if (:reported? pub) :republished :published) pub) true])\n   933\t\n   934\t    (not (:reported? pub))\n   935\t    (if (pos? (:waiting pub))\n   936\t      [pub nil false]\n   937\t      (let [pub (assoc pub :ended (ending pub))\n   938\t            pub (assoc pub\n   939\t                       :reported? true\n   940\t                       :last [(result pub) (:ended pub)]\n   941\t                       :due (+ (:reading node) (:delay pub)))]\n   942\t        [pub (report :published pub)\n   943\t         (or (= :acknowledged (result pub)) (some? (:ended pub)))]))\n   944\t\n   945\t    :else\n   946\t    (let [pub (close-cycle node pub)\n   947\t          pub (assoc pub :ended (ending pub))\n   948\t          now [(result pub) (:ended pub)]]\n   949\t      (if (= now (:last pub))\n   950\t        [pub nil false]\n   951\t        [(assoc pub :last now) (report :republished pub)\n   952\t         (or (= :acknowledged (result pub)) (some? (:ended pub)))]))))\n   953\t\n   954\t\n   955\t(defn- retire\n   956\t  \"`node` without the publication `pub`; its queue entries no other live\n   957\t   holder needs are dropped.\"\n   958\t  [node pub]\n   959\t  (-> node\n   960\t      (update :pubs (fn [pubs] (filterv #(not= (:id pub) (:id %)) pubs)))\n   961\t      (release-entries (:order pub) (:id pub))))\n   962\t\n   963\t\n   964\t(defn- displace\n   965\t  \"Beyond `:max-repairing`, retire the oldest repairing publications.\"\n   966\t  [node]\n   967\t  (loop [node node\n   968\t         events []]\n   969\t    (let [repairing (filter repairing? (:pubs node))]\n   970\t      (if (<= (count repairing) (limit node :max-repairing))\n   971\t        [node events]\n   972\t        (let [oldest (assoc (first repairing) :ended ::displaced)]\n   973\t          (recur (retire node oldest)\n   974\t                 (conj events (report :republished oldest))))))))\n   975\t\n   138\t(defn- result-text\n   139\t  \"A publication's result (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.5.6): when it is not\n   140\t   acknowledged, the count of failed blobs, the first reason, and whether\n   141\t   the node is retrying.\"\n   142\t  [node {:keys [result blobs peers failed repairing? ended]}]\n   143\t  (if (= :acknowledged result)\n   144\t    (str \"acknowledged: sent to \" peers \" peers\")\n   145\t    (str (if (= :partial result)\n   146\t           \"PARTIAL: the manifest was sent; \"\n   147\t           \"NOT acknowledged: \")\n   148\t         (reason-text node (first failed))\n   149\t         \"; \" (count failed) \" of \" blobs \" blobs not sent\"\n   150\t         (cond\n   151\t           repairing? \"; retrying while the node is open\"\n   152\t           ended (str \"; not retrying (\" (get ended-text ended (str ended)) \")\")\n   153\t           :else \"; not retrying\")\n   154\t         \"; the local copy is durable\")))\n   155\t\n   340\t                                                 (contains? modules m))\n   341\t                                        m)))\n   342\t                                  (mapcat :free ps)))))\n   343\t        undefined (first (remove defining exports))]\n   344\t    (if undefined\n   345\t      (refusal :yin.link.publish/undefined-export {:export undefined})\n   346\t      (let [collected (loop [ms (set (map (comp :m defining) exports))]\n   347\t                        (let [ps (filterv #(contains? ms (:m %)) programs)\n   348\t                              unrequired (first (remove requiring (linked ps)))\n   349\t                              more (-> ms\n   350\t                                       (into (keep (comp :m defining))\n   175\t(def ^:private publisher-lines\n   176\t  [\"(def f (fn [x] (+ x 4200)))\"\n   177\t   \"(def base 7)\"\n   178\t   \"(def g (fn [] (+ base 1)))\"\n   179\t   \"(require (quote yin.link))\"\n   180\t   \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))\"\n   181\t   \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.store) (quote [g]))\"])\n   182\t\n    88\t(def dht-module-name\n    89\t  \"The module `(require 'dao.space.